  "explains": "Cache.get changes. The name get is defined six times in non-test code (Cache, Registry, Settings, Lookup, Memo and the handler InvoiceController.get), more than distinct_max = 3: it is not distinctive, so it is recorded and no code is linked to the change by the word get. The importers of Cache are linked by the type: StatusController (the field cache and its constructor use the type) and WebConfig (the bean method). In StatusController the handler status uses the field cache and is reached, with GET /ledger/v1/status; the handler flags only calls flags.get(mode), the get of a map, which shares the word and nothing else: it is not reached. Registry, Settings, Lookup and Memo define their own get: they are not callers. The route is called by fetchStatus and reaches the screen /status.",
